Update resource path validation pattern to
{code:java}
^(?:[^~<>:\\|\\\"\\?\\*\\.\\/\\\\]+(?:[/\\\\][^~<>:\\|\\\"\\?\\*\\.\\/\\\\]+)*)?$  {code}
so we can't assign multiple resources to a given agent class with the same resource name and different path as a string but with the same at file system level. Eg ./folder/subfolder folder/subfolder folder/./subfolder folder/././subfolder and so on.

Without this fix, we can assign multiple resource with the same path at file system level. As a result, un-assigning one of them will make other resource assignments inaccessible.

