When GetElasticsearch processor has an incoming connection, and the document id is an expression, this results in expression evaluating to null when the processor runs without a flow file. This can happen in a clustered NiFi setup when there are more nodes in the cluster than the number of flow files in the queue.

For example, when there is a flow file in the queue, the processor's onTrigger is invoked on all nodes (even the ones that don't have a flow file) resulting in some nodes throwing an error.

 This can be handled by short-circuiting the onTrigger method like many core processors do
{code:java}
        FlowFile input = null;
        if (context.hasIncomingConnection()) {
            input = session.get();

            // If we have no FlowFile, and all incoming connections are self-loops then we can continue on.
            // However, if we have no FlowFile and we have connections coming from other Processors, then
            // we know that we should run only if we have a FlowFile.
            if (input == null && context.hasNonLoopConnection()) {
                return;
            }
        }
{code}

